        "What helped most was showing the route in the order the person would follow it. If I’d pointed straight at the desk from where I was standing, they might still have joined the wrong queue. I learnt that a small gesture can make spoken directions clearer, especially when people can’t hear every word. I’d still check that they’ve understood if the route is complicated, perhaps by asking which way they’re going first."
